you comes down the stair into the hedge.
The Hedge (binary, 5 rings of 10 spokes, seed 3). Find the far gate. Type help for the words.
The Mouth of the Hedge
A stair goes up behind you. A plate is set in the hedge beside it.
Sunwise, the way runs three paces and turns right.
> read
The hedge is rings round a well. The ways are in, out, sunwise and widdershins. The hedge leans inward. Every square seems to open in, or sunwise, or both.
> study
The hedge is rings round a well, and a ring comes back to where it began. Its ways are in, out, sunwise and widdershins; there is no north here. Every square opens in or sunwise. Walk in and sunwise and you come to the well from anywhere, where one wall, the seam, runs from the well to the rim and stops you. From there, one way leads out to every square.
> look
The Mouth of the Hedge
A stair goes up behind you. A plate is set in the hedge beside it.
Sunwise, the way runs three paces and turns right.
> north
There is no north in this hedge. Its ways are in, widdershins, out, sunwise, and up and down where there is a stair.
> in
The hedge is in the way.
> cast (go north)
The spell does not hold (chibi): (go north): go needs one direction: in widdershins out sunwise ahead back left right up down
> cast (until (gate?) (if (open? in) (go in) (if (open? sunwise) (go sunwise) (stop))))
The spell holds (chibi). It runs one step a turn; stop ends it.
